<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Batecor half year loss narrows, scraps div.</title>
<headline>Batecor half year loss narrows, scraps div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     1.6 loss    vs 6.3 loss</p>
<p>    Headline shr (cts)    2.9 loss    vs 9.5 loss</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 nil	   vs 3.5</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   1.84 loss   vs 5.08 loss</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   1.51 loss   vs 4.67 loss</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.37	  vs 0.12</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   5.12	  vs 8.57</p>
<p>    Turnover (cont ops)   229.26	vs 208.68</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     1.52 gain   vs 5.19 loss</p>
<p>Full name: Bateman Industrial Corp Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The firm said the loss was mostly a result of the company's investment in Computer Alliance, which was sold during the period.</p>
<p>It added that the full benefits of a restructuring at the group would probably not be seen until the next financial year.</p>
<p>Batecor said consideration would be given to the resumption of dividend payments at the end of the year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
